<BibleSubsetHub
  id="books"
  metaTitle="Books of the Bible Coloring Pages — All 66, Free PDF"
  description="All 66 books of the Bible on six coloring pages, one per group, from the Law to Letters and Revelation. Each book is a tile to color as your child learns it."
  h1="Books of the Bible Coloring Pages"
  crumb="Books of the Bible"
  intro="These six pages list all 66 books of the Bible in order, one page for each group: the Law, History, Poetry, the Prophets, the Gospels and Acts, and the Letters and Revelation. Every book is a tile to color, under a picture that hints at what that part of the Bible is about. Children learning the books in order can color a tile each time they get one more book right. Print the group you are working on, or all six in one PDF."
  sections={[
    { heading: "How the Bible’s books are grouped", body: "The Old Testament has 39 books and the New Testament 27. These pages use a grouping often taught in Sunday school: 5 books of the Law (Genesis to Deuteronomy), 12 of History (Joshua to Esther), 5 of Poetry and Wisdom (Job to Song of Solomon), and 17 of the Prophets (Isaiah to Malachi); then 4 Gospels plus Acts, and 21 Letters followed by Revelation. Learning six groups is easier than learning 66 names in one long list, because each group is short and has its own picture." },
    { heading: "A coloring game for learning the order", body: "Start with the Law: five books, one page. Your child says the books in order, and each time they get further than before, they color the next tile. When all five are colored, move on to the History page. The longest page, the Letters, has 22 tiles; split it over a few weeks. Keep finished pages together in order so your child can see how much of the Bible they know." },
    { heading: "If your Bible has more books", body: "Catholic and Orthodox Bibles include additional Old Testament books, such as Tobit and the books of Maccabees, so their tables of contents are longer than 66. These pages follow the 66-book order found in most Protestant Bibles." },
  ]}
  faq={[
    { q: "How many books are in the Bible?", a: "66 in most Protestant Bibles: 39 in the Old Testament and 27 in the New Testament. Catholic and Orthodox Bibles include more." },
    { q: "Are all 66 books on these pages?", a: "Yes, across the six pages. The full-set PDF prints them all in order." },
    { q: "Why are Lamentations and Daniel with the prophets?", a: "In most Protestant Bibles, Lamentations comes right after Jeremiah and Daniel right after Ezekiel, so they are usually learned along with the prophets." },
    { q: "Is there a single-page list of all the books?", a: "Not yet; each page covers one group so the tiles are big enough to color. Print all six for the complete set." },
  ]}
